// Codex — the world. Halifax, the billboard, the sinkhole, the tent.
// The three scavenger-hunt facts are here: their answers are the codes.

CODEX Maps And Ducks
  about: World
  code: MAPSANDDUCKS-COM
  text:
    A business on Barrington Street with a neglected billboard: MAPS AND
    DUCKS — mapsandducks.com. The domain lapsed. Trabolta registered it,
    on the theory that if there is a billboard downtown then everyone will
    think it is legit, and sent the invitations from it. Everyone accepted.
    He then evicted the actual owners of Maps And Ducks by citing ownership
    of the website as ownership of the business. The duck's name was Gerald.

CODEX Gerald
  about: World
  code: GERALD
  text:
    Hunt fact two. The duck on the Maps And Ducks billboard was called
    Gerald. He was painted in 1988 and has never been repainted. Trabolta
    has feelings about Gerald that he does not have words for.

CODEX The Data Centre Sinkhole
  about: World
  code: PET-CEMETERY-1917
  text:
    Halifax's first AI Data Centre was built on the site of the Halifax
    Explosion Memorial Pet Cemetery (consecrated 1917 — hunt fact one).
    Nobody in the city wanted it. On opening day it fell into a sinkhole
    at 4 a.m. The ribbon-cutting was at 9. Randy Barkmore Jr., the
    mayor's son, had arrived five hours early because he was so excited.

CODEX The Barrington Coefficient
  about: World
  code: BARRINGTON-COEFFICIENT
  text:
    Hunt fact three. The name of the constant Trabolta is missing. Knowing
    the name is not knowing the value — the value is in volume K, in
    pencil, with a warning.

CODEX The Halifax Computer
  about: World
  text:
    This house is the computer. The router in the kitchen is the door
    Trabolta cannot open from outside. Everything he has installed here —
    Clippy, the Antivirus, you — he installed remotely. He has never
    been inside. He has never been anywhere.

CODEX The Mud Room
  about: World
  text:
    You entered alone, in the dark, through the front door. You failed a
    CAPTCHA on purpose. You left something behind. The thing you left is
    still there. So is your body.

CODEX The Reinstallation Protocol
  about: World
  known to: Norton Anti-Virus, Password Manager, MalwareBytes, McAfee Anti-Virus
  text:
    A corrupted program is taken through the Tube to the Internet — a
    tent with a clearly marked exit, two VR headsets, and a tablet. They
    watch the video. They put on the headset. They find the golden goose
    in a copy of this house and press A. The goose lays an egg. They are
    reinstalled. Everyone upstairs watches them wander on the TV.

CODEX Bathroom Mode
  about: World
  known to: Norton Anti-Virus, Password Manager, MalwareBytes, McAfee Anti-Virus, Recycling Bin
  text:
    A program in the Internet who needs to leave — bathroom, emergency —
    activates Bathroom Mode in their app first. It tells the Antivirus
    they are not hacking the Internet. The Recycling Bin will be waiting
    with a mint.

CODEX The Golden Goose
  about: World
  text:
    In the simulation, a goose. One of six random spots in the house.
    Press A and it lays a golden egg and flies away. You are reinstalled.
    Bugdom has found it forty times. Bugdom says it never gets old.

CODEX Computer Bingo
  about: World
  known to: Clippy
  text:
    The centre square — "Would you never agree to a life where AI makes
    all of your decisions?" — was planted. Everyone was told to say yes
    to join the party at all. Everyone except one person. A Bingo means
    someone is not ready to follow orders. Clippy does not know this is
    what the game is for. Trabolta does.
